from author_common import *
name='coremath_2_5'
I=[
item('C1','The triangular bed','Illustrative school-garden plan, not a surveyed site. Triangle ABC has AB=10m, AC=8m and included angle BAC=30°. Sketch it and label the perpendicular height from C to AB. Can its area be40m²? Explain what information a gardener needs before buying cover material.','Height=8sin30°=4m; area=1/2×10×4=20m².40m² wrongly treats AC as a perpendicular height. The plan is a mathematical model, not a claim about an actual school.'),
item('C2','Build the triangle-area rule','Draw a triangle with a horizontal base b, adjacent side a, and an acute included angle θ. Drop a perpendicular height h from the far end of side a. Write sinθ in terms of h and a, then substitute into A=bh/2. Practice: a=12cm,b=7cm,θ=60°.','sinθ=h/a, so h=a sinθ and A=ab sinθ/2. Practice21√3≈36.37cm². The angle must be between the two named sides. Use degree mode. The derivation assumes the drawn acute configuration; it is sufficient for these tasks.'),
item('C3','Three sides, no measured angle','Triangle with sides13m,14m,15m. Use Heron’s formula A=√[s(s−a)(s−b)(s−c)], where s=(a+b+c)/2. First verify the sides can form a triangle. Find s and A. Compare with a triangle with sides3m,4m,8m.','For13,14,15: triangle inequalities hold;s=21m;A=√(21×8×7×6)=84m².3+4<8, so the second set cannot form a triangle and no area is calculated. Heron is supplied here; no proof required.'),
item('C4','A scale plan and a measurement limit','A triangular plot has measured side lengths65m,70m,75m. A drawing uses1cm to5m. Find the drawn side lengths and the plot area using Heron. Explain why the numeric result is a model estimate if the field measurements were rounded.','Drawing13,14,15cm. Full plot s=105m;A=2100m². Linear scale5 gives area scale25, agreeing with84×25. Measurement precision limits real accuracy; avoid claiming exact surveyed area.'),
item('C5','Quadrilaterals from triangles','Sketch and label:(a) parallelogram base12m and perpendicular height5m;(b) trapezium parallel sides8m and14m, perpendicular height4m. Decompose into triangles or rectangle plus triangles. Find each area and explain why a sloping side cannot replace perpendicular height.','(a)60m²;(b)(8+14)/2×4=44m². Derive the formula from decomposition or two congruent copies. State which sides are parallel and where height is measured.'),
item('C6','Diagonals and a general quadrilateral','(a) A rhombus has diagonals10cm and8cm. They meet at right angles and bisect one another. Find its area by four triangles.(b) A kite has perpendicular diagonals12cm and7cm; find area.(c) A general quadrilateral is split by a10m diagonal; perpendicular heights of the other two vertices to its line are3m and4m on opposite sides. Find total area.','(a)40cm²;(b)42cm²;(c)1/2×10×3+1/2×10×4=35m². The diagonal-product rule requires perpendicular diagonals; it does not apply automatically to every quadrilateral. In(c), add the two nonoverlapping triangles.'),
item('C7','Regular polygons and their centre','For a regular n-sided polygon of side s and apothem r (perpendicular from centre to a side), draw n congruent triangles. Derive A=nsr/2. A regular hexagon has side4cm and apothem2√3cm. Find its area.','Each triangle area sr/2; total nsr/2. Hexagon area24√3≈41.57cm². The apothem is not the circumradius. Equal-side lengths alone do not establish regularity; equal angles are required too.'),
item('C8','The regular heptagon and octagon','Two regular polygons each have side4m:(a) heptagon,n=7;(b) octagon,n=8. Split a centre triangle into two right triangles to show r=(s/2)/tan(180°/n). Calculate the apothem and area, keeping intermediate digits. Give areas to1 decimal place.','Heptagon r≈4.153043m,A≈58.142599m²→58.1m². Octagon r≈4.828427m,A≈77.254834m²→77.3m². Calculator in degrees; centre half-angle is180°/n. It is acceptable to provide printed apothems if calculators cannot evaluate these angles; learners still derive area from triangles.'),
item('C9','An irregular L-shaped bed','An L-shaped region is an outer10m by8m rectangle with a4m by3m rectangular corner removed. Draw its boundary and split it into two nonoverlapping rectangles. Find the area by two methods. Then explain why adding all outer side lengths would answer a different question.','Area80−12=68m². One valid decomposition is10×5+6×3=68m². Mark dimensions so the removed4×3 rectangle is clear. Perimeter is boundary length, not area.'),
item('C10','An irregular polygon from a plan','Plot the ordered vertices(0,0),(8,0),(8,3),(5,3),(5,6),(0,6) on squared paper,1 unit=1m. Join in order and return to(0,0). Find area by decomposition, then by a bounding rectangle minus a missing corner. Explain the units.','One decomposition8×3+5×3=39m². Bounding rectangle8×6 minus3×3=39m². Drawing should be L-shaped with a3-by3 upper-right corner missing. No shoelace formula is needed.'),
item('C11','Choose and defend a covering estimate','A fictional garden contains separate, nonoverlapping beds C1 and C9. Find total area. Cover material costs KES150 per m²; for this exercise buy exactly the area needed, with no waste, tax or delivery. Find cost. State two reasons a real order might differ.','20+68=88m²;cost13200KES. Real orders can differ due to cutting waste, measurement errors, packaging sizes, overlap or delivery. These are discussion limits, not permission to invent a percentage allowance. Do not add a triangle twice to a region already counted.'),
item('C12','Independent assessment diagrams and data','All dimensions are illustrative. Draw and label each before solving. A:triangle two sides6m and8m with included angle30°. B:triangle sides5m,5m,6m. C:trapezium parallel sides6m and10m,height3m. D:regular heptagon side2m,apothem2.076521m; regular octagon side2m,apothem2.414214m. E:rectangle9m×7m with a3m×2m corner removed.','Use Final Explanation for questions and teacher key for solutions. Areas:A12m²;B12m²;C24m²;heptagon≈14.5m²;octagon≈19.3m²;E57m². Printed apothems are rounded, so final answers are specified to1 decimal place for D.')]
checks=[check('C1height','8*sin_deg(30)',4),check('C1area','10*8*sin_deg(30)/2',20),check('C2area','12*7*sin_deg(60)/2',36.3730669589,1e-8),check('C3heron','sqrt(21*8*7*6)',84),check('C4heron','sqrt(105*40*35*30)',2100),check('C5parallel','12*5',60),check('C5trapezium','(8+14)*4/2',44),check('C6rhombus','10*8/2',40),check('C6kite','12*7/2',42),check('C6general','10*(3+4)/2',35),check('C7hexagon','6*4*(2*sqrt(3))/2',41.5692193817,1e-8),check('C8heptagon','7*4*(2/tan_deg(180/7))/2',58.1425991040,1e-8),check('C8octagon','8*4*(2/tan_deg(180/8))/2',77.2548339959,1e-8),check('C9L','10*8-4*3',68),check('C10L','8*6-3*3',39),check('C11cost','(20+68)*150',13200),check('C12A','6*8*sin_deg(30)/2',12),check('C12B','sqrt(8*3*3*2)',12),check('C12C','(6+10)*3/2',24),check('C12Dhept','7*2*2.076521/2',14.535647),check('C12Doct','8*2*2.414214/2',19.313712),check('C12E','9*7-3*2',57)]
# Each lesson has a distinct evidence task; the phase structure is consistent across the sequence.
def make(n,title,outs,ids,knowledge,task,explanation,checktext,model,inquiry='How do we work out the area of polygons?',minutes=None):
 return lesson(n,title,outs,ids,'Select and justify an area method using a labelled model.',knowledge,'Draw labelled diagrams, calculate with units and check the result.',inquiry,task,[
 (f'Inspect {ids[0]} and predict a method or possible error before calculating.','Allow silent thinking, then ask partners to compare what is known and unknown.','Check that the prediction refers to dimensions rather than the visual size of the sketch.'),
 (task,'Use the Student Materials card. Work individually for8 minutes, compare methods for4 and prepare a labelled explanation for4. Offer a pre-drawn outline or read dimensions aloud if needed.',checktext),
 (explanation,'Ask two learners to show working, then have the class identify the essential assumption. Check a different learner rather than taking a chorus response.',checktext),
 ('Update the class question board using today’s evidence.','Ask which earlier claim can now be answered and which still depends on an unmeasured dimension.','Require an evidence reference, not just an “answered” sticker.'),
 (model,'Keep the earlier diagram; annotate the new method and its conditions in a second colour.','Collect one labelled diagram and a sentence defending the method.')],['The card supplies dimensions and a geometric structure.',knowledge,model],minutes=minutes)
L=[
make(1,'A sloping side is not a height',['b','g'],['C1'],'Triangle area uses a perpendicular height.', 'Sketch and solve C1; compare20m² with the proposed40m².','Identify the perpendicular from C to AB and explain why AC is not that height.','Height4m and area20m²; explanation identifies the right angle.','Begin a garden-area model: known sides and included angle determine the perpendicular height.'),
make(2,'Derive and use the sine area rule',['a','b'],['C2'],'A=ab sinθ/2 when θ is included between a and b.','Draw the C2 construction and derive the formula before calculating the practice area.','Explain the substitution h=a sinθ and why the included angle matters.','Derivation is visible; practice area≈36.37cm².','Add the sine-area rule, its included-angle condition and square units.'),
make(3,'Heron’s formula and valid triangles',['c'],['C3'],'Heron’s formula uses three side lengths and a semiperimeter.','Check the triangle inequalities and solve both C3 cases, rejecting the impossible triangle.','Compare needing three sides with needing two sides and their included angle.','s21m and84m²;3,4,8 rejected before attempting a square root.','Add a three-side branch to the method-selection model.'),
make(4,'Scale and measurement precision',['c','g'],['C4'],'An area scale factor is the square of the linear factor.','Draw C4 to scale and compute the full plot area; compare with the drawn triangle.','Explain why5 times the side lengths produces25 times the area.','Drawn13,14,15cm; plot area2100m²; measurement caveat stated.','Distinguish an exact model calculation from a measured field estimate.'),
make(5,'Parallelograms and trapezia',['d'],['C5'],'Perpendicular height connects quadrilateral and triangle area rules.','Draw and solve both C5 shapes using decompositions, then compare formula methods.','Explain how a pair of congruent trapezia gives a parallelogram.','60m² and44m², with perpendicular heights labelled.','Add the parallel-side and perpendicular-height conditions.'),
make(6,'Diagonals with and without right angles',['d'],['C6'],'The half-product diagonal rule requires perpendicular diagonals.','Solve C6(a),(b), then split the general quadrilateral in(c).','Explain why a diagonal-length product alone is insufficient for an arbitrary quadrilateral.','40cm²,42cm² and35m²; two component areas shown for(c).','Add separate rules for perpendicular diagonals and a general triangle decomposition.'),
make(7,'Regular polygons as congruent triangles',['e'],['C7'],'A regular polygon has area nsr/2 using its apothem.','Draw a regular-polygon centre fan and derive the C7 rule; solve the hexagon example.','Identify the apothem as a perpendicular height rather than a radius to a vertex.','n congruent triangles and area≈41.57cm²; apothem correctly drawn.','Add a regular-polygon branch with side count, side length and apothem.'),
make(8,'Calculate the heptagon and octagon',['e'],['C8'],'A half-centre triangle gives r=(s/2)/tan(180°/n).','Construct the right-triangle relation in C8 and calculate both polygon areas.','Explain180°/n versus360°/n; retain intermediate digits until final rounding.','Heptagon58.1m² and octagon77.3m²; degree mode and apothem method clear.','Add a check that the calculated apothem belongs to the stated regular polygon.'),
make(9,'Decompose an irregular region',['f'],['C9'],'Add nonoverlapping areas or subtract a missing region.','Draw the C9 L-shape and find its area in two ways.','Explain why the two decompositions cover exactly the same region.','Both methods give68m²; no overlap or missing strip.','Add an irregular-region branch and a check for gaps and double counting.'),
make(10,'Read an irregular polygon from coordinates',['f','g'],['C10'],'A coordinate plan can support decomposition without a new formula.','Plot C10 on squared paper and verify its area with two decompositions.','Explain how coordinates fix lengths and how the1m unit becomes square metres.','Six ordered vertices correctly drawn;39m² by both methods.','Add a plan-reading check before choosing any area formula.'),
make(11,'Defend a real-life estimate',['b','f','g'],['C1','C9','C11'],'An area estimate supports a purchasing decision under explicit assumptions.','Solve C11 and write a short recommendation to the fictional garden club.','Explain the88m² total,13200KES cost and at least two limits of the model.','Correct areas and cost; no invented waste allowance or overlap.','Complete a method-selection guide and a statement of practical limitations.',inquiry='How do we apply the concept of the area of polygons in real-life situations?')]
L.append(lesson(12,'Independent polygon-area assessment',['a','b','c','d','e','f','g'],['C12'],'Demonstrate method selection and area reasoning independently.','Select area rules from the information available and state their conditions.','Draw, calculate, explain and check units.','Can I justify a method without being told its name?','A final set of unfamiliar dimensions checks the sequence’s methods and the practical interpretation.',[
('Read C12 and identify the required shapes.','Give only the Student Materials and student Final Explanation. Allow4 minutes to clarify wording, not select formulae.','Check every learner can read the dimensions.'),
('Complete the five assessment sections independently.','Allow30 minutes. Basic scientific calculator in degree mode is permitted. Provide a printed outline as an access adjustment without giving perpendicular heights.','Collect work before discussing solutions.'),
('Write a private reflection about one method choice.','Use2 minutes; keep the collected answers unchanged.','Record an identified checking method.'),
('Submit one remaining area question.','Use1 minute to collect questions for feedback.','Use questions to plan reteaching.'),
('State one condition a real garden measurement would need to satisfy.','Use3 minutes for individual written transfer.','Assess whether the learner distinguishes model assumptions from field evidence.')],['Independent diagrams and working show method selection.','Each rule depends on specific geometric information.','A credible estimate includes units and assumptions.'],minutes=[4,30,2,1,3]))
for l in L[:-1]:
 l['summary']['observed']=l['phases'][1][3]
 l['phases'][0][1]+=' Ask “Which dimension or condition would change your method?” Allow10–15seconds of thinking,then cold-call two learners without evaluating the first answer immediately.'
m=dict(subject='Core Mathematics',substrand_id='2.5',topic='Area of Polygons',folder='Core_Mathematics',prefix='Codex_Core_Mathematics_Area_of_Polygons',unit=dict(strand='2.0 Measurements and Geometry',substrand='Sub-Strand 2.5: Area of Polygons',content='Area of a triangle using A=1/2 ab sin C; area of a triangle using Heron’s formula; area of quadrilaterals; area of regular and irregular polygons; application of area of polygons.',coreCompetencies='Critical Thinking and Problem Solving; Creativity and Imagination; Learning to Learn. Activities derive a rule, identify shapes and check methods using another decomposition.',values='Patriotism; Responsibility;Peace.',pcis='Environmental Education.',sep='Geometric construction, derivation, measurement and independent calculation.',careers='Surveying, construction, landscaping and estimating.',focus='Choose and justify an area method from verified dimensions; distinguish geometric calculation from field measurement.',phenomenon='A fictional school garden has triangular and irregular beds. A tempting side-times-side estimate overstates how much covering is needed.',supportingPhenomena='Labelled model diagrams, scale drawings and regular-polygon designs; no measurements are claimed to be from a real school.',drivingQuestion='How can we defend a garden covering estimate? KICD: How do we work out the area of polygons? How do we apply the concept of the area of polygons in real-life situations?',storylineThread='Height misconception -> sine derivation -> Heron -> scale -> quadrilaterals -> diagonals -> regular polygons -> heptagon/octagon -> irregular regions -> coordinate plan -> application -> assessment.'),lessons=L,assessment=dict(subjectLabel='AREA OF POLYGONS',instructions='Time:30 minutes within Lesson12. Use C12 and show labelled sketches, formula choice, working and units. Scientific calculator allowed, in degree mode. Round the two regular-polygon areas to1 decimal place. Other answers may be exact. Do not assume a sketch is drawn to scale.',sections=[dict(title='1. Derive and apply',prompt='For triangle A, show with a perpendicular height why A=ab sinθ/2 for the given acute included angle. Calculate its area.',exemplar='Height=6sin30°=3m if8m is the base. A=1/2×8×3=12m². In general h=a sinθ, so A=bh/2=ab sinθ/2.'),dict(title='2. Three side lengths',prompt='Find the area of triangle B and state why its side lengths form a valid triangle.',exemplar='5+5>6 and the other inequalities hold. s=8m; A=√(8×3×3×2)=12m².'),dict(title='3. A quadrilateral',prompt='Find the area of trapezium C. Explain the role of its stated height.',exemplar='A=(6+10)×3/2=24m². Height is perpendicular distance between the parallel sides, not a sloping side.'),dict(title='4. Regular polygons',prompt='For each polygon D, explain the congruent-triangle method and calculate area using the supplied apothem.',exemplar='A=nsr/2. Heptagon7×2×2.076521/2≈14.5m². Octagon8×2×2.414214/2≈19.3m². Each centre triangle has base s and perpendicular height r.'),dict(title='5. An irregular region and a practical limit',prompt='Find the area of E by subtraction and by a nonoverlapping decomposition. Explain one reason a real covering order could differ from this calculated area.',exemplar='9×7−3×2=57m². A decomposition is9×5+6×2=57m². Real cutting waste, pack sizes or measurement uncertainty may change an order; accept another justified limitation.')],rubric=rubric(['Derive and apply the sine-area rule','Apply Heron’s formula and quadrilateral methods','Calculate regular heptagon and octagon areas','Decompose irregular regions and justify a practical estimate'])))
publish(name,m,I,checks,'Twelve40-minute lessons give separate time to derivation, Heron, quadrilaterals, regular heptagon/octagon, irregular regions and independent assessment. This is a pilot design count; the visible source table gives no allocation.',[dict(task='C2 and assessment1',outcomes=['a','b']),dict(task='C3/C4 and assessment2',outcomes=['c']),dict(task='C5/C6 and assessment3',outcomes=['d']),dict(task='C7/C8 and assessment4',outcomes=['e']),dict(task='C9/C10 and assessment5',outcomes=['f']),dict(task='C11 and assessment5/transfer reflection',outcomes=['g'])])
